# Build context filter for frontend/Dockerfile (BuildKit reads <Dockerfile>.dockerignore next to it).
# The context is the repository root, but the image needs only frontend/ and the DIN 4023 assets:
# everything else is left out first, then those two are let back in.
*
!frontend/
!assets/din4023_patterns/

# Never sent, even from inside the folders above.
**/.git
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/dist-*
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
**/blob-report
**/coverage
**/.vite
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.log
frontend/docs/

# Env files (also .env.sample and .env.local): a stray frontend/.env must never switch the build to
# sample mode or carry a value into the image. The Dockerfile sets the build's env itself.
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Data, uploads and runtime folders: never part of an image (already outside the folders above,
# listed so a wider rule later cannot let them in).
backend/
local/
storage/
uploads/
HKBoreholeChallenge*
**/HKBoreholeChallenge*
**/*.zip
